HUMAN: Round 9 analysed — full HUD revamp to the user's sci-fi mock; layout spec below, hard UI invariants apply.
NOTE mock-spec what="Target design (user mock, dark slate translucent panels, 1px light borders, cyan/teal accents, amber highlights, small-caps labels, mono numerals): TOP-LEFT brand chip [wing glyph + CANYON FLIGHT SIM + version]. TOP-CENTER compass ribbon: tick marks + cardinal/degree labels scrolling with heading, center caret + heading chip '015°'. TOP-RIGHT: credits chip (map to score points) + transient '+45 AMMO' reward toast slot; sub-row FPS + PING chips with 4-bar signal glyph (PING only in multiplayer, else hide). LEFT CLUSTER: card of three big numerals SPD/ALT/HDG with unit sublabels; below it small WIND chip (map: wind gust system if present, else hide). RIGHT CLUSTER: quad card HULL/SHD/ENG/FUEL each with label + % + slim progress bar (HULL=plane.health, SHD=plane.shield, ENG=engine temp derived 60+throttle*35+damage.engine*40 °C, FUEL=cosmetic slow drain from 100 refreshed on reset — no fuel system exists, keep visual only). RIGHT COLUMN: CURRENT OBJECTIVE panel (course director target text + distance, existing #course-director data) and NEARBY CONTACTS panel (top 3-4 traffic targets: colored diamond glyph, callsign, type, distance — REPLACES the floating per-target text labels which currently clutter the sky; keep the in-world diamond brackets, kill the floating text tags). RIGHT-BOTTOM: circular radar (2D canvas ~180px: N-up, rings at 1KM/3KM, player triangle center, contact diamonds colored by hostility, faint sweep wedge; 10Hz update). BOTTOM-CENTER: NEXT CHECKPOINT chip (distance) flanked by 4 small icon buttons (map: waypoint toggle, target cycle, camera mode, plane cycle). BOTTOM-LEFT: FLIGHT MODE dropdown chip (existing flight profile/style options) + three square chips BOOST/GUNS/FLARES (map: boost=engine surge availability or throttle%, GUNS=ammo state READY/count, FLARES=missile count relabeled MSL). BOTTOM-RIGHT: COMMS panel (static waveform strip + CH 1 pill + latest flashStatus message line as comms text; NO avatar image required). CENTER: two curved bracket arcs flanking the reticle (SVG or CSS border arcs), vertical speed tape left of center + altitude tape right of center (tick columns w/ value chips '404 KTS'/'FT 165'), small pitch-ladder marks near bottom center above the water line."
NOTE ui-invariants what="I3: NO backdrop-filter on persistent HUD (compositor cost — hard rule from perf history). Existing JS writes these ids (grep hudCache and updateHUD): speed/alt/hdg/hull/shield/ammo/etc — plan must either keep the same element ids in the new structure or update every writer site (prefer keeping ids). DOM text writes must stay cached/dirty-checked like the existing pattern (textContent only when changed, 10Hz for readouts). Radar canvas: its own <canvas>, 2D context, update at 10Hz max, no per-frame allocation. Touch controls / mobile media queries must not break (menu + HUD share breakpoints ~720/800px). Existing panels (P graphics panel, race panel, review panel, target course director) get restyled to the same design language but keep their DOM/JS contracts."
FIND F16 sev=H tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html#"top strip / #instruments" what="current HUD is functional pills but user wants full mock fidelity" fix="rebuild HUD chrome per mock-spec NOTE while preserving every JS data contract; stage the work: (1) CSS design system (panel/chip/label/bar classes), (2) top bar + left/right clusters restructure keeping ids, (3) compass ribbon (new, driven by plane heading each frame via transform translateX — cheap), (4) contacts panel + kill floating target text tags, (5) radar canvas, (6) bottom row chips + comms, (7) center arcs + tapes; each stage independently bootable" ref=cascade/00-task.txt dep=-
DONE stage=F find=1 note=single-mega-finding-with-staged-fix tok~=720
